A||||17||ChadMan||Please give me your 2 cents||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||02-18-2000||06:02 PM||||Last Sunday, I looked at an 85 GT (4-sp, 100K miles) for sale about 15 min from my house.<P>The bad news:  The black paint was terribly faded and has been keyed.  Decklid requires a hearty slam to shut b/c the iron hoop it catches on appears bent (maybe used to support car during clutch job?).  Hood slightly crooked.  Filthiest Fiero V6 engine I've ever seen, and red paint peeling from intake plenum and valve covers.  Clutch engages smoothly, but engages right off of floor - probably needs hydraulic components.  Trunk absolutely filthy.  Interior needs center console, driver's seat, headliner and sunroof seal.  "Check Engine" came on when engine reached normal operating temp, but no driveability problems (EGR?).  Pulls to left under braking.  A/C inoperative.  E-brake inoperative.  Shocks/struts nearly shot.<P>The good news:  Engine sounds very healthy.  Oil clean.  No exhaust manifold leaks.  Ran strong, even on a cold rainy morning.  Despite bad paint, all body panels (except maybe nose) in good shape including 1/4 windows and "ground effects" panels.  Frame appears straight and rust-free - no apparent collision damage.  Shifts smoothly into all 4 gears - owner claims he replaced clutch mechanicals himself and I found no reason to think he was lying.  Coolant clean - no cooling system problems.  Headlight motors work.  Steering tight (balljoints/steering rack/tie rod ends apparently A-OK) but needs alignment.  All gauges work.  Factory radio/tape deck/speakers work.<P>He's asking $2000 OBO but seemed ready to deal.  If you were Fiero shopping (and aren't we all) what would you pay for this car?<P>Thanks in advance for your help and for reading this far! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||02-18-2000||06:30 PM||||Sounds like a good restoration project, but I would not pay 2,000 for it. I'd offer him 500 at the most. I say this because from what you described this fiero needs a LOT of TLC. What I would really do if I where you is look for an 88 model year, they are so much better than the other years as far as mechanical parts. I've owned an 87 coupe and now have an 88 formula and I've driven an 87 and 88 GT. If you have patience there are better deals out there and there are 88's for sale. Good luck… ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||02-18-2000||07:19 PM||||2K does sound a mite high, but one note on the clutch '85s had the alu pedal and if that one still has it it's bent. $30 for a steel one and clutch all fixed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||02-18-2000||09:42 PM||||$2000 is what I gave for my 88 GT. It is kind of rough, but sounds like it is in as good or better shape than the 85. I would wait or offer much less. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||11:35 PM||||I paid $400 for my '85 GT (still have to pick it up) with custom paint, aftermarket wheels, good body, fair interior.  The only problem is that the motor needs a crank and bearings. <P>Anybody want to donate any time to the Monkeymans Fund for Fallen Fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||02-19-2000||12:26 AM||||Wasn't it "Don't let a good Fiero go bad!" -or something like that?<P>Based on what I've seen here (Atlanta), I would only give $500-1000, max, if I were in the market.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||william_thorniii||02-19-2000||12:39 AM||||Chadman,<P>I will be selling my 85 GT in the spring.  It will have under 70k on the clock.  I will have replaced by then: carpeting, driver's seat cover (some list members have seen the one on it and would question why I would replace it), 120 mph speedo, new headliner (I can't take credit for this... it was done at a shop), Hurst shifter, fairly clean trunk carpet, very good interior, pm, pdl, psteering (just seeing if anyone is reading) , vista vent, wind deflector, new dew strips, battery, plugs, wires, cap, rotor, ign. module, yadda.. yadda.. yadda.  I can tell you that I would also like to slap a coat of paint on it.  The factory red has a bad case of crows feet.  Why am I putting this time and $ into a car that I am going to get rid of?  1) It does not have enough miles for me.  I bought my 87 CP with under 50 on the clock and am running it to death.  Every time I drive my cars, I watch my odometer more than anything else.  I realize that these are not exactly "low mileage" cars, but what can I say... I'm paranoid.  2)  I really thought that the red would grow on me.  Sorry guys (even you Chad), I know that red seems to be the most popular color, but it is just not me.  I am not ready to try to change the color, that is far too hard when one is as anal as I am.  Oh did I mention that the thing passed E-check without a cat?  That's right it is catless.  It has a cherry bomb welded in the place of the cat too.  I was not sure how it would do, but I had room to spare in every category including nox!  <P>If you are serious let me know and I can hold off on most of the parts to keep the price down, or I can continue to deck it out.  I would REALLY like to sell it to someone that I trust like you though.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000007||william_thorniii||02-19-2000||12:42 AM||||OOOOPS!  I almost forgot that I am currently working on retro-fitting a factory performance sound system to the car. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
